>>
Rule 1 (image must be at least 3-D)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 3
>>
Rule 2 (lower bound must be non-negative)
{v_1 : float} |= v_1 ≥ 0
>>
Rule 3 (upper bound must be greater than lower bound)
{v_1 : float, v_2 : float} |= v_2 > v_1
>>
Rule 5 (tensor shape matches given tuple shape)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= ndim(v_1) = v_2.len ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = v_2[i]
>>
Rule 8 (image must have valid shape for contrast adjustment)
{v_1 : tensor} |= shape(v_1, 0) ≥ 1 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) ≥ 1 ∧ shape(v_1, 2) ≥ 1
